            "text": "{\n  \"primary_meaning\": \"Protection, refuge, and divine sheltering care, often representing God's loving provision and deliverance.\",\n  \"primary_basis\": [\n    \"Psalm 91:4\",\n    \"Ruth 2:12\",\n    \"Exodus 19:4\",\n    \"Psalm 36:7\",\n    \"Matthew 23:37\"\n  ],\n  \"alternatives\": [\n    {\n      \"meaning\": \"Speed, swiftness, and mobility, often related to the swiftness of divine judgment, angelic movement, or spiritual elevation.\",\n      \"basis\": [\n        \"Isaiah 40:31\",\n        \"Jeremiah 48:40\",\n        \"Habakkuk 1:8\"\n      ],\n      \"prominence\": \"common\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"meaning\": \"Healing and restoration, specifically associated with the fringes or corners of a prayer garment (tzitzit).\",\n      \"basis\": [\n        \"Malachi 4:2\",\n        \"Numbers 15:38\",\n        \"Zechariah 8:23\"\n      ],\n      \"prominence\": \"common\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"meaning\": \"Divine glory, presence, and overshadowing majesty, represented by the wings of the Cherubim covering the Mercy Seat.\",\n      \"basis\": [\n        \"Exodus 25:20\",\n        \"Isaiah 6:2\",\n        \"Ezekiel 1:8\"\n      ],\n      \"prominence\": \"common\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"meaning\": \"The extremities, boundaries, or four corners of the earth.\",\n      \"basis\": [\n        \"Isaiah 11:12\",\n        \"Job 37:3\"\n      ],\n      \"prominence\": \"minority\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"has_settled_consensus\": true,\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"notes\": \"The Hebrew word kanaph translates to both wing and extremity or edge, such as the corner of a garment. While its most dominant symbolic use in Christian devotion is divine protection under the shadow of God's wings, its literal meaning as a garment's edge provides a rich secondary symbolic layer regarding healing, particularly in interpreting passages like Malachi 4:2 alongside the New Testament accounts of individuals being healed by touching the hem of Christ's garment.\"\n}",
